  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release of the PublicFunction.AsyncDataBase library - A fully asynchronous version of the database toolkit.\n\n      ✨ Key Features in this version:\n      - **Microsoft SQL Server**: Async `SQLService` for executing stored procedures and commands with non-blocking I/O.\n      - **Redis**: Async `RedisManager` for key-value, hash, list, and set operations using StackExchange.Redis.\n      - **MongoDB**: (To be documented) Async infrastructure for MongoDB interactions.\n      - **MySQL**: (To be documented) Async infrastructure for MySQL database interactions.\n      - **Oracle**: (To be documented) Async infrastructure for Oracle database interactions.\n      - **RabbitMQ**: (To be documented) Async infrastructure for RabbitMQ message queuing.\n\n      📦 How to use:\n      All methods are designed with async/await patterns to improve scalability and performance in high-concurrency scenarios.\n\n      📚 Complete documentation and usage examples are available in the project repository:\n      https://github.com/rayanabniro/PublicFunction/tree/main/PublicFunction.AsyncDataBase",
